    runtime: a type in a pattern bounded by a set is no final non-member
    
    The library declares each kept form a member of its set by a pattern bounded by the set (`Compiled{Z} where Z <: X`,
    `Dynamic{Z} where Z <: X`). `Compiled{S}` is in `X` where `S` is, so whether it is rests on `S`'s memberships, and
    its non-membership's cell, the pair (`Compiled{S}`, `X`), is met by no membership of `S`: inference folded
    `Compiled{S} <: X` and `Dynamic{Y} <: X` to `false` as final and kept it after `S` joined `X` (found by the
    set-folds report's library mode, shapes `compiled` and `dynamic`). Now a concrete type on whose chain a pattern's
    entry has a variable bounded by a type in which an open set occurs is no final non-member: the negative is not
    folded (`chain_has_set_bounded_pattern` in `jl_membership_final`).
    
    Reference: compiler §4.8, §6.9.
    Test: experiments/implementation/w171/gates/n48_kept_form_not_final.jl.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

